---

## Test Smell Audit — `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1.0 · **.NET 10** · **Integration scope** (`[TestCategory("Integration")]`)

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High | 3 | 3 |
| Medium | 1 | 1 |
| Low | 0 | 0 |
| **Total** | **4** | **4** |

---

### Findings by Severity

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Smell 3: Sleepy Test

**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);   // blocks the thread for 3 seconds
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Integration calibration:** Even for integration tests, `Thread.Sleep` is a smell. It makes the test slow (3 s per run), and the value is arbitrary — too short causes false failures, too long wastes CI time.

**Fix — poll with a timeout:**
```csharp
var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow.AddSeconds(5);
while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
{
    if (_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
        break;
    await Task.Delay(100);
}
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky CI failures; suite slows linearly as more timing-dependent tests are added.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Smell 1: Conditional Test Logic

**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 94)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Integration calibration:** Not mitigated — this is structural ambiguity, not integration-test scope. The `if/else` means one branch is never exercised per run. You don't know *which* behavior was verified.

**Fix — separate into two deterministic tests:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasDiscountRate()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", 0.1m));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.IsInstanceOfType<PremiumUser>(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(((PremiumUser)loaded).DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Hidden coverage gap — if the production type ever changes, the untested branch silently passes.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Smell 4: Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // No assertions — passes even if every insert silently fails
}
```

**Integration calibration:** Not mitigated. The test name implies "no errors," but it never verifies state. It gives false confidence.

**Fix — verify the outcome:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Complete false confidence — 100 % pass rate with 0 % behavioral verification.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette (Extended Catalog)

**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);          // assertion 1
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);   // assertion 2
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email); // assertion 3
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);      // assertion 4
```

4 assertions, none with a message parameter. A failure in CI shows only `Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<...>` — you must read the code to know which property was wrong.

**Integration calibration:** Slightly downgraded — multi-property verification is expected in integration tests. Still worth fixing for CI diagnostics.

**Fix — add message parameters:**
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be auto-assigned");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower diagnosis when CI fails — especially painful in matrix builds.

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✅

The remaining tests are well-structured:

| Test | Why it's good |
|------|---------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear Arrange-Act-Assert; focused on one behavior |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single post-condition asserted (`Assert.IsNull`) |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count assertion (3) is self-documenting after inserting 3 items — **not** a Magic Number smell |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Clean `async`/`await` with a single count assertion |

The `[TestInitialize]`/`[TestCleanup]` fixture is **not** General Fixture — both `_connection` and `_repository` are used by every test method.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Test | Effort | Why first |
|----------|-------|------|--------|-----------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free (High) | `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` | ~2 min | Prevents a false-pass — highest risk-to-effort ratio |
| 2 | Conditional Logic (High) | `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` | ~10 min | Eliminates a hidden coverage gap |
| 3 | Sleepy Test (High) | `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` | ~10 min | Removes flakiness and 3 s of CI wall-time |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette (Medium) | `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` | ~2 min | Improves CI diagnostics — quick win |

**Bottom line:** 4 of 8 tests have smells. The three High-severity findings — assertion-free, conditional logic, and sleep — are the ones that actively undermine test-suite trustworthiness. The good news: the other half of the suite is clean, and every fix listed above is straightforward.
